{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 96}
{tag: Easy}
{tag: Singalong}
{meta: language en}

{comment: The chords never leave the first position, so it works just as well around a fire as it does on a porch.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From this [G]valley they say you are [C]going
We will [G]miss your bright eyes and sweet [D7]smile
For they [G]say you are taking the [C]sunshine
That has [G]brightened our [D7]pathway a[G]while
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [C]love me
Do not [G]hasten to bid me a[D7]dieu
Just re[G]member the Red River [C]Valley
And the [G]cowboy who [D7]loved you so [G]true
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Won't you [G]think of the valley you're [C]leaving
Oh how [G]lonely, how sad it will [D7]be
Oh think [G]of the fond heart you're [C]breaking
And the [G]grief you are [D7]causing to [G]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
As you [G]go to your home by the [C]ocean
May you [G]never forget those sweet [D7]hours
That we [G]spent in the Red River [C]Valley
And the [G]love we ex[D7]changed 'mid the [G]flowers
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
